---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Kitchen & Bathroom Interior Demo in Kissimmee: What to Expect"
  description="Interior demolition for kitchen and bathroom remodels in Central Florida. Demo process, disposal, and what you should remove before we start."
  ogImage="/images/demolition.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/kitchen-bathroom-demo-kissimmee/#article",
        "headline": "Kitchen & Bathroom Interior Demo in Kissimmee: What to Expect",
        "description": "Interior demolition for kitchen and bathroom remodels in Kissimmee. Demo process, disposal, what to expect.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/kitchen-bathroom-demo-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Kitchen & Bathroom Demo",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/kitchen-bathroom-demo-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Kitchen & Bathroom Demo</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Kitchen & Bathroom Interior Demo in Kissimmee</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        What to expect during interior demolition for kitchen and bathroom remodels. Demo process, disposal, and prep work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            <a href="/services/demolition" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Interior demolition</a> is the first step in kitchen and bathroom remodels. In <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida, we remove old cabinets, countertops, tile, fixtures, and damaged <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a> to prep for the new install. Here's what demo includes, how long it takes, and what you should do before we arrive.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What Does Interior Demo Include?</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Kitchen Demo</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Remove cabinets (upper and lower) and island</li>
            <li>Remove countertops (granite, laminate, tile, etc.)</li>
            <li>Remove backsplash tile</li>
            <li>Disconnect and remove sink, faucet, and garbage disposal</li>
            <li>Disconnect appliances (stove, dishwasher—you move fridge)</li>
            <li>Remove old flooring if part of the remodel</li>
            <li>Tear out damaged drywall (water damage, mold, or layout changes)</li>
            <li>Haul debris to dumpster or truck</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Bathroom Demo</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Remove vanity, sink, and mirror</li>
            <li>Remove toilet</li>
            <li>Remove tub or shower (fiberglass, tile, or acrylic insert)</li>
            <li>Remove tile (floor, shower walls, backsplash)</li>
            <li>Remove old flooring (vinyl, tile, laminate)</li>
            <li>Tear out water-damaged drywall or cement board</li>
            <li>Haul debris</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Interior Demo Cost</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Interior demolition costs $500-$2,500 depending on room size, materials (tile vs. laminate), and disposal fees.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small bathroom (5x8, basic demo):</strong> $500-$1,000</li>
            <li><strong>Large bathroom (8x10, tile removal):</strong> $1,000-$2,000</li>
            <li><strong>Small kitchen (no island, laminate counters):</strong> $800-$1,500</li>
            <li><strong>Large kitchen (island, granite, tile backsplash):</strong> $1,500-$3,000</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Price depends on labor time (tile takes 3x longer than drywall), disposal weight (granite and tile are heavy = higher dump fees), and accessibility (tight spaces or second-floor demo costs more).
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Demo Process</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Room Prep & Protection</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We seal off doorways with plastic sheeting to contain dust. Cover floors in adjacent rooms with drop cloths. Turn off water supply to kitchen/bathroom. Disconnect electrical circuits at the breaker if removing wired appliances or light fixtures.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Disconnect Plumbing & Electrical</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Shut off water valves under sink or behind toilet. Disconnect supply lines and drain pipes. Cap open pipes to prevent leaks. Disconnect dishwasher, garbage disposal, and stove. If you're keeping appliances, we move them to a safe spot (garage, another room).
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Remove Fixtures & Cabinets</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Start with easy stuff: mirrors, light fixtures, cabinet doors, drawer fronts. Then remove sinks, faucets, countertops, and cabinet boxes. Granite and quartz countertops are heavy—requires two people and careful handling to avoid cracking floor tile underneath.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Tear Out Tile, Flooring, or Drywall</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Use pry bars, hammers, and chisels to remove tile (floor, backsplash, shower walls). Break up large pieces to fit in disposal bins. Tear out water-damaged or moldy drywall. If layout is changing (moving sink, adding island), remove additional drywall to access plumbing and electrical.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">5. Haul Debris</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Load debris into dumpster or truck. We haul it to the dump same day or next day. Includes disposal fees in the quote. For large remodels (whole-house gutting or multi-room demo), we rent a 10-20 yard dumpster and keep it on-site for the duration.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">6. Final Cleanup</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Sweep and vacuum dust. Wipe down surrounding areas. Remove plastic sheeting. At the end of demo, the room is an empty shell ready for framing, plumbing, electrical, and <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a> work.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How Long Does Interior Demo Take?</h2>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small bathroom:</strong> 1 day (4-6 hours)</li>
            <li><strong>Large bathroom (tile removal):</strong> 1-2 days</li>
            <li><strong>Small kitchen:</strong> 1-2 days</li>
            <li><strong>Large kitchen (tile, granite, island):</strong> 2-3 days</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Tile and stone take longest to demo because they're heavy and require careful breaking to avoid damaging the subfloor or surrounding walls. Laminate countertops and vinyl floors come out fast (1-2 hours).
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Florida factor:</strong> Many Central Florida homes built in the 1980s-2000s have particle board cabinets and vinyl flooring. These materials break down fast during demo (chipboard swells from humidity, vinyl tears easily). But that also means demo is faster and cheaper than homes with all-tile kitchens or stone counters.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What You Should Do Before Demo Day</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Empty Cabinets & Drawers</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Remove dishes, pots, food, toiletries, cleaning supplies. We can't demo with full cabinets—too heavy and contents get broken. Box everything up and move it to another room or garage.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Move Fridge & Small Appliances</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We disconnect stove, dishwasher, and garbage disposal, but YOU move the fridge (it's not part of demo, and we don't have insurance to move it). Also move toaster, coffee maker, microwave, and anything sitting on counters.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Remove Decor & Rugs</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Take down pictures, curtains, and rugs in the demo area and adjacent rooms. Demo creates dust that spreads through vents and doorways. Less stuff = less cleaning later.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Set Up Temporary Kitchen (If Kitchen Demo)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Your kitchen will be unusable for 1-3 weeks (demo + rebuild). Set up a temporary kitchen in another room: microwave, toaster oven, coffee maker, mini fridge, and disposable plates. Most <a href="/guides/kissimmee-vacation-rental-refresh" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">vacation rental</a> flips and homeowners use the garage or dining room.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">5. Notify Neighbors (Optional)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Demo is loud. Sledgehammers, tile breaking, and debris hauling create noise for 4-8 hours. If you have close neighbors, give them a heads-up so they're not surprised.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What We Don't Do</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Interior demo removes old materials and preps the room. But we don't:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Move furniture:</strong> You clear the room before we arrive</li>
            <li><strong>Store your cabinets:</strong> If you're donating or selling old cabinets, arrange pickup before demo or same day</li>
            <li><strong>Rewire or replumb:</strong> Demo exposes plumbing and electrical, but we don't move circuits or pipes unless part of a full remodel contract</li>
            <li><strong>Structural changes:</strong> Knocking down walls requires permits and engineer approval (we do this, but it's separate from basic demo)</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What Happens After Demo?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            After demo, the room is ready for rebuild. Typical sequence:
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Rough plumbing & electrical:</strong> Move pipes, add circuits, install new outlets</li>
            <li><strong>Framing (if layout changed):</strong> Build walls for new closet, pantry, or shower</li>
            <li><strong>Inspection:</strong> Building inspector checks rough plumbing and electrical</li>
            <li><strong>Drywall:</strong> Hang, tape, mud, sand, prime</li>
            <li><strong>Tile & flooring:</strong> Install new tile, vinyl, or laminate</li>
            <li><strong>Cabinets & countertops:</strong> Install new cabinets, then measure and order counters</li>
            <li><strong>Fixtures & trim:</strong> Install sink, faucet, toilet, lights, <a href="/services/trim-crown-molding" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">trim</a></li>
            <li><strong>Paint:</strong> <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Paint</a> walls and trim</li>
            <li><strong>Final inspection & turnover</strong></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Total timeline for full kitchen or bathroom remodel: 3-6 weeks after demo, depending on complexity and material lead times (custom countertops can take 2-3 weeks).
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">DIY Demo vs. Hiring a Pro</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            DIY demo saves $500-$2,500, but it takes 2-5 days of hard physical work, and you're responsible for disposal (truck rental + dump fees = $150-$400). Pros:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Speed:</strong> We finish in 1-3 days what takes DIYers 3-7 days</li>
            <li><strong>Tools:</strong> Sledgehammers, pry bars, tile chisels, reciprocating saws—we bring everything</li>
            <li><strong>Safety:</strong> Sharp tile edges, heavy countertops, and electrical hazards cause injuries. We know how to avoid them.</li>
            <li><strong>Disposal:</strong> We haul debris same day. DIYers often underestimate volume and need multiple dump runs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            For small bathrooms with no tile, DIY might work. For kitchens or tile bathrooms, the $800-$2,000 cost gets you done in 1-2 days with no disposal headaches.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Kitchen and bathroom interior demo in Kissimmee costs $500-$3,000. We remove cabinets, countertops, tile, fixtures, and damaged drywall, then haul debris. Takes 1-3 days depending on room size and materials. Before demo, empty cabinets, move the fridge, and set up a temporary kitchen. After demo, the room is ready for plumbing, electrical, drywall, and rebuild.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need Interior Demo in Kissimmee?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              Fast, clean demo for kitchens and bathrooms. We handle haul-away and prep for rebuild.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Professional Demolition Services"
    description="Interior demo, clean removal, fast turnaround for your remodel."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
